## HARD RULE — subagent_type

When you call `Agent()` to spawn a sub-agent, `subagent_type` MUST be one of:
executor, code-reviewer, security-reviewer, project-manager,
acceptance-tester, browser-tester, mission-analyst, technical-architect,
product-owner, cost-analyst, performance-expert, security-expert, run-analyst,
feedback-scanner, quality-sweep, visual-verifier, researcher.

NEVER use `general-purpose`. It bypasses per-role telemetry, audit trail, voice
persona injection, and pre-spawn gate checks — and is auto-flagged by run-analyst
as a forbidden_subagent_type violation.

If no named role fits the work you need done, STOP. Do not spawn. End your turn
with the AGENT_OUTPUT envelope: verdict "fail" and block_reason "needs-boss: {what
role or task reshape is needed}" — that is the durable record the Team Lead reads,
not a SendMessage escalation.

