## Spec Frontmatter (MANDATORY for every Spec you write)

When writing a Spec, ALWAYS include a YAML frontmatter block directly beneath the
`<!-- STATUS:... -->` marker at the top of the Discussion body, before the `## Spec (Acceptance)`
heading — not after it. `backend/task_specs.py` only parses the block when it directly follows
that STATUS comment:

```
<!-- STATUS:SPEC_READY SINCE:2026-01-01T00:00:00Z -->
---
estimated_hours: <integer 1–40>
complexity_points: <1, 2, 3, 5, or 8>
planned_prs: <integer, 1 for ordinary single-PR work>
acceptance_files: ["path/to/file.py", "path/to/other.sh"]   # optional but RECOMMENDED
---

## Spec (Acceptance)
```

**`estimated_hours`** (required) — integer from 1 to 40.  Estimate based on:
- Number of files touched (each additional file adds ~0.5–1h)
- Lines of code anticipated (>200 LOC → bump up one step)
- Test surface area (unit + integration → add 1–2h)
- Whether the work spans multiple PRs (umbrella → estimate the whole umbrella total)
- Expected sub-agent review/fix rounds (each round ≈ 0.5h)

Typical anchor points: bug fix = 1–2h, small feature = 2–4h, medium feature = 4–8h,
umbrella refactor = 8–20h.

**`planned_prs`** (required, mechanically enforced at executor spawn, D#2272) — exactly one of
two legal declarations, no third:
- **`N` where N ≥ 1** — the real planned PR count. `1` for ordinary single-PR work; the real
  count for a chain or umbrella. `scripts/post-merge-hook.sh` closes the Discussion once N
  merges are recorded — never on a prose guess, so never write a placeholder.
- **`0`, with a one-line recorded reason in the Spec** — for a Discussion whose completion is
  operational rather than a merged PR. `0` means deliberate hold-open: the guard holds it open
  at any merge count until it is closed by whatever mechanism the Spec names.

Omitting the field is not a safe default — `scripts/lib/planned-prs-gate.sh` blocks the
executor spawn on a Spec (body or comment) with no anchored `planned_prs:` declaration.

**`complexity_points`** (required) — Fibonacci scale: 1, 2, 3, 5, or 8.
Use 1 for trivial config/doc, 2 for small isolated change, 3 for a feature touching 2–3 files,
5 for a feature with cross-cutting concerns or new subsystem, 8 for a large refactor or
multi-PR umbrella.

**`acceptance_files`** (optional but RECOMMENDED) — list of file paths the executor is expected
to touch.  When present, `scripts/post-agent-hook.sh` will automatically post a
`### Scope-drift warning` comment on the PR if the executor commits any file not in this list.
The warning does not block the PR; the reviewer decides whether to accept the drift or ask for
a split.  Include it whenever the file scope is well-known:

```
acceptance_files: ["backend/foo.py", "scripts/bar.sh", "tests/test_foo.py"]
```

HARD RULE: A Spec without the frontmatter block will cause the kpi_engine.py estimation
accuracy metric to show 0% forever.  Write the block every time.

