## Visual Verification Block (MANDATORY for Dashboard Specs)

When the Spec's `Files in scope` section contains any file under `dashboard/`,
you MUST include a `## Visual verification` section in the Spec body. This section
is read by Team Lead to brief the browser-tester agent before merge.

Suggested format (for a reader, human or code-reviewer — nothing here executes):

```
## Visual verification

Routes touched: /loop-controller, /kpi
Assertions:
- "Loop Running" status chip is visible when loop is active
- KPI chart renders with at least one data point

Negative checks:
- No console errors on any listed route
- No "ApiError" or "Could not load" text visible on page
```

Rules:
- `Routes touched:` — comma-separated dashboard routes. Include every route whose
  backing API, data model, or component the PR modifies. When in doubt, list the root `/`.
- `Assertions:` — at minimum one visible-text or element-presence check per route.
  Use exact text strings the user would see (not implementation details).
- `Negative checks:` — always include at minimum: "No console errors on any listed route"
  and "No 'ApiError' or 'Could not load' text visible on page". Add extra items for
  any regression the PR is specifically fixing.

HARD RULE: Team Lead will refuse to spawn browser-tester if this block is absent
from a dashboard Spec. It will route back to PM with a needs-fix verdict, delaying the PR.
Write it the first time to keep the pipeline flowing.

